Package: plateforce
Title: Force-Plate Jump Kinetics that Carry Their Method
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Alex", "Harrison", email = "alex@saturdaymorning.fit",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: Computes jump kinetics from a vertical ground reaction force
    trace. Every value carries the method that produced it: the rule, its
    published parameters, its citation and the choices made upstream of it.
    Ten published ways of computing one jump height disagree by 3.51 cm on
    244 real trials, against the 1.98 cm training effect the source study
    was built to detect, so the method is reported with the number.
    Authorship and copyright of the bundled Rust sources are listed in the
    AUTHORS file of the installed package.
